                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "HTC VIVE review.\nTo the point: This is a brawler VR game. That means you will be swinging your arms a lot. Mainly throwing punches and doing a few special moves here and there depending on your abilities. It is very physical and quite a work out when doing it for long periods. From what I played the game is fun. The layout of the level was kind of, well, repetative but that is not the highlight of the game. The fighting is. The mobs get harder as one would expect the farther you go in the game. There is a story but it is a little hard to follow as the game is not natively made for English audiences but you get an idea of what you are striving for. You can read and hear the story. There are abilities to get and upgrade after collecting some things. The fighting rather than story interested me most. It does take some time to get used to the fighting and the use of your movement to use to your advantage but as you go it grows on you. For the price of the game I think it can be fun for those looking to get into some real fist fighting in VR. The graphics are good, models well done, and the game ran smooth on my setup. When I play more and if there is much more content to this after my last save point then I will update my review to a higher rating. For now to be fair 6/10 is what I give it. \n\nHere is a 4k video of my first game play. I could not have my camera showing because of some problems with my recording/streaming software so it is hard to really see what I am doing but you should hear my comments as I go and get an idea of what the game is about. Take note my frustration is always high when I first play a VR game. That is just me. I do like this game but it is very physical as I stated. Enjoy the show. ;-)\n\nhttps://gaming.youtube.com/watch?v=1vRNnH6So78&feature=share",
